1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.
我是你的中国旅游专家

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
One country and your teacup share a name.
一个国家，和你的茶杯同名

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
In English, fine porcelain is just "china."
英文里，瓷器就叫 china

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
Fired near 1,300°C until clay turns to glass.
烧到近1300°C，泥变成玻璃

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
Thin enough to see light straight through.
薄到能透光

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
The secret clay is kaolin — named for a village.
秘密在高岭土，得名一个村

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
Gaoling, by Jingdezhen — imperial kilns 1,000 years.
高岭，挨着景德镇——御窑千年

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
Double-tap if you'd drink from this.
想用它喝茶的，点个赞

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,800
Blue-and-white sailed the seas and became China itself.
青花漂洋过海，成了中国的名片

10
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,000
★ Expert Tip: Tap a bowl — real porcelain rings like a bell; a dull thud means a crack.
内行贴士：轻敲瓷碗，真瓷像铃、闷响=有裂

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Porcelain or silk — which would you carry home?
瓷器还是丝绸，你带哪个回家
